@@ -348,6 +348,7 @@ None of these changes the default. Each is read from the environment when the ga
 | `VICTORY_WINDOW_SECONDARY=x,y` | Opens the game window on the display that holds the desktop point `x,y`, for layouts with more than one extra display (a Sidecar iPad beside two monitors, say). |
 | `VICTORY_FRAME_WAITS=1` | Logs title pacing, queue waits and presentation wall time in release and diagnostics builds. |
 | `VICTORY_SHADER_OPT=2` | Folds defined integer constant arithmetic and comparisons before DXIL emission. Off by default and keyed separately for shader and pipeline caches. |
+| `VICTORY_HALVES_F64_COUNT=1` | Enables exact FP64 counts of 1.0 across two host waves in proven exchange blocks. Requires halves exchange and uses its own shader and pipeline cache keys. |
 
 The frame wait report prints after a completed PresentX call at intervals of at least five seconds. Times are milliseconds per completed PresentX, including calls that did not display a picture. Queue pumping, submission settling and host presentation are phases inside PresentX. Frame sleeps and fence waits can run on other threads and overlap.
 
